---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { doctor, site } from '../data/site.js';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What information this website collects, how consultation records are handled, and your rights over your data."
  slug="privacy"
  updated="2026-10-17"
  intro="What this website collects, what the practice holds about patients, and what you can ask for."
>
  <div class="note note-warn">
    <h3>Before publishing</h3>
    <p>
      This policy is a working draft prepared alongside the website. It should be reviewed by a
      lawyer familiar with the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and with medical
      records requirements before the site goes live, and the Data Protection Officer details
      below must be completed.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {doctor.name}, {doctor.qualifications}, {doctor.registration}, practising at clinics in Narela
    and Rohini, Delhi, and providing online consultations. Contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What the website collects</h2>

  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    If you agree to analytics when asked, we record which pages are visited, how far down a page
    people scroll, and which buttons are used. This is used to understand which pages are useful.
  </p>
  <p>
    This analytics data is deliberately limited. It does not include your name, phone number,
    email address or anything you type. Specific health conditions are recorded only as broad
    categories, never as the individual page where that would identify a health concern with a
    person. If you decline, no analytics are loaded at all.
  </p>

  <h3>If you contact us</h3>
  <p>
    When you message on WhatsApp, call, or email, we receive whatever you choose to send —
    typically your name, contact number and a description of your concern. This is used to
    respond to you and to arrange a consultation.
  </p>

  <h2>Patient records</h2>
  <p>
    If you attend a consultation, in person or online, a clinical record is created. It contains
    your history, examination findings, any photographs you provide or that are taken with your
    consent, test results, and prescriptions issued.
  </p>
  <p>
    Clinical records are confidential. They are not shared with family members, employers or
    anyone else without your consent, except where disclosure is required by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    Records are retained in line with medical record-keeping requirements in India. Online
    consultations are additionally governed by the Telemedicine Practice Guidelines, which
    require that identity, consent and the consultation record are documented.
  </p>

  <h2>Photographs</h2>
  <p>
    Photographs form part of your clinical record and are stored with it. They are never used on
    this website, on social media, in teaching or in any other public setting without your
    separate, specific, written consent — and that consent can be withdrawn.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else processes your data</h2>
  <p>
    The website is hosted by a third-party hosting provider. Analytics are processed by a
    third-party analytics provider, only with your consent. Payments, when taken, are processed
    by a payment provider and card details are never held by us. Where any of these are located
    outside India, data may be processed outside India.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 you may:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask what personal data we hold about you</li>
    <li>Ask for inaccurate data to be corrected</li>
    <li>Ask for data to be erased, subject to medical record retention requirements</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent you previously gave, including for analytics and for photographs</li>
    <li>Raise a grievance, and escalate it to the Data Protection Board of India</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To make any of these requests, write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changing your analytics choice</h2>
  <p>
    Your choice is stored in your own browser. Clearing your browser's site data for this website
    will make the question appear again, and you can answer differently.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is not directed at children. Patients under 18 are consulted with a parent or
    guardian present, and their records are handled with the same confidentiality.
  </p>

  <h2>Grievance contact</h2>
  <p>
    [To be completed before publication: name and contact details of the person responsible for
    data protection queries.]
  </p>
</Page>
